Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day: a month flipped. By
4 October the desk had **412 reports**.

**Merged as one issue.** The parser reads dates month first, and our tenants write the day
first. The fix is queued.

<Callout kind="warn">
Closed 5 October, split. Read the reports, not their subjects, and this ticket holds three problems:
the parser ([#1](https://github.com/piotrek-kaminski/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1), fixed), the booking-v3 form hint
([#2](https://github.com/piotrek-kaminski/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2), won't fix: form retired) and one-day moves
across time zones ([#3](https://github.com/piotrek-kaminski/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3), still open).
See [#4471 · three problems, not one](/kb/incidents/4471-split).
</Callout>

